{
  // Type-check the VFS image builders. There was no config covering `images/`
  // at all, so every recipe under it was unchecked: a broken import or a
  // signature drift surfaced only when a builder was RUN, which needs a full
  // sysroot and a kernel and takes hours.
  //
  // Built before the change it is meant to check, deliberately. Lane V's own
  // hazard list says a gate written afterwards gets shaped to pass, and lane Y
  // is about to repoint thirteen of these files onto a new interface.
  //
  // NOT YET WIRED AS A BLOCKING GATE. Its first run found four type errors
  // under `images/`: one introduced by this lane and fixed, and three that
  // predate it. TWO REMAIN, both in one file —
  //
  //   images/vfs/scripts/staged-product-inputs.ts
  //     `keyof typeof STAGING_FLAGS` is a Map's METHOD names, not its keys
  //   images/vfs/scripts/staged-product-inputs.ts
  //     `kind` stays `unknown`; the ternary chain narrows it for a reader but
  //     not for the compiler
  //
  // The third is FIXED, 2026-09-13, as a side effect of moving
  // build-source-rootfs-shell-image.ts onto the Rust filesystem: it passed a
  // StatResult where `{ ino, generation? }` was expected, and the identity
  // comparison there now takes the module's 64-bit inode numbers instead of
  // silently comparing a bigint to a number.
  //
  // Each remaining one is a real defect in a production build script, and
  // fixing them means behaviour judgement in code this lane did not otherwise
  // touch — a scope question for the maintainer, not a coding one. A gate with
  // a baseline of two cannot detect the third, which is why this is recorded as
  // unwired rather than wired with an allowance.
  //
  // It is useful as it stands: run it and require that the errors under
  // `images/` are exactly those two. Line numbers are deliberately not quoted
  // any more — they moved once already and a stale number reads as a different
  // defect.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "lib": ["ES2024", "ES2024.SharedMemory", "DOM"],
    // Resolved from host/, which is where this repository installs its
    // TypeScript toolchain; there is no node_modules under images/.
    "typeRoots": ["../host/node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["vfs/**/*.ts", "rootfs/**/*.ts"]
}
